- defines(v1, ...): Range only contains `{"Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site"}`, omitting the `"Customer returns the items to the store"` alternative explicitly listed in the source description.
- branch(b1, XOR) and precedence(b1, n3): Declared as an exclusive split but only defines one outgoing precedence edge, omitting the control-flow path for `"Customer returns the items to the store"`.
- defines(v3, ...): Range only contains `{"Customer does not return the missing items"}`, omitting the `"Customer returns the missing items"` alternative explicitly listed in the source description.
- defines(v5, ...): Range only contains `{"Items are stored for future orders"}`, omitting the `"Items are packed for an existing order"` alternative explicitly listed in the source description.
- branch(b5, XOR) and precedence(b5, n14): Declared as an exclusive split but only defines one outgoing precedence edge, omitting the control-flow path for `"Items are stored for future orders"`.
- action(n10, ...) and action(n11, ...): Payloads describe conditional outcomes/states (`"Items are repaired and added into inventory"`, `"Items can't be repaired and are discarded"`) rather than executable process steps, misusing the `action` element type.
- precedence(c1, n13) through action(n14, ...): Forces every process path through `"Email customer with replacement charges"` before termination, contradicting the source which ties replacement charge emails to specific missing/discarded scenarios or explicitly places the final email after completion (`"Once again, when the process is complete, it ends. The customer is then emailed with replacement charges..."`).

Structural Check
- [S1] STC9 failed: Each branch node must have exactly one incoming and at least two outgoing edges. | Node `b1` has in=1 and out=1. | Node `b3` has in=1 and out=1. | Node `b5` has in=1 and out=1. | DSL: branch(b1,XOR); branch(b3,XOR); branch(b5,XOR)
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `['Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site']`. | Variable `v3` has an invalid range `['Customer does not return the missing items']`. | Variable `v5` has an invalid range `['Items are stored for future orders']`.
- [S3] STC15 failed: Every variable used in a guard must be formally defined. | Guard `v1 = 'Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site'` on `b1 -> n3` uses undefined variable `v1`. | DSL: guard(b1,n3,"v1 = 'Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site'")
- [S4] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> c1` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b3 -> c1` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b4 -> n11` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b5 -> n14` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.

